    "modifiedAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "mx_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -324
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Music Box\n\nA disc music box: pins on a turning disc pluck the comb as they pass it (top right), the inner rings low notes, the outer high. Click on the disc to put in a pin where you click, or click a pin to take it out. New tune (or N) composes another one from noise, C clears the disc; Speed and the Scale are on the canvas.\n\nHow it works: the pins are a list of (angle on the disc, ring) kept from frame to frame by a Write* → Read* pair (\"pins\"), and Integrate turns the disc at Speed. Plucks finds the pins that crossed the comb since the last frame; their rings become notes through Scale, shared out to three Bells (two sine partials → Envelope each) that Mix into a reverb. Compose makes a tune from noise; Edit pins adds and removes them.",
        "width": 470,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
